      "inspection": "Restoration architect front-on seaward photograph individually inspected: open classical colonnade ahead of glass, two curved terraces, glazed upper room, white tower lattices and silver domes."
    },
    {
      "sourceUrl": "https://find-an-architect.architecture.com/purcell-architecture-ltd/canterbury/penarth-pier-pavilion",
      "downloadUrl": "https://s3-eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/riba-faa-practiceimages/ProjectImages/3486_145445_2.jpg",
      "artist": "Phil Boorman, credited on image; Purcell project submission",
      "license": "Not stated; research viewing only, no source pixels redistributed.",
      "actualSha256": "sha256:ad9b94a6875e3a22687f14c3af399c314fd83df50fd4f27b7fd85cd070e93ad4",
      "inspection": "Restoration architect full south-side photograph individually inspected: four original-domed corner towers, four tall dormer windows along zinc barrel roof, long ridge vents/11 ribs, small square clock on cantilever bracket at landward south tower, own cream low shop wing and concrete under-pavilion structure; town promenade buildings excluded."
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://cadwpublic-api.azurewebsites.net/reports/listedbuilding/FullReport?id=13355&lang=en",
      "inspection": "Primary designation read: about200m pier,15m historic landing-stage width, cast-iron original center and concrete landward/landing ends; two boarded shelters/head ticket office. Main1929 concrete pavilion: four tapering corner towers with pinnacled Moghul roofs/deep bracketed eaves, large diaper grilles/two smaller paired tiers, convex landward lobby/concave classical shop wings, curved seaward glazed colonnade,11-bay barrel roof/four tall side windows/ridge ventilators. Legacy parenthetical seaward(W) is a compass typo; actual mapped/aerial seaward direction ESE is used.",
      "scopeCorrection": "Do not reconstruct lost1931 wooden concert hall; surviving shore pavilion predates fire."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://find-an-architect.architecture.com/purcell-architecture-ltd/canterbury/penarth-pier-pavilion",
      "inspection": "Restoration architect Purcell project statement read:2013 conservation retained/repaired ferro-concrete and added shiny fish-scale metal roof coverings; ends/internal spaces altered for cafe/observatory/cinema. Two external photographs individually inspected as credited; no photograph pixels embedded."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/enjoying/Coast-and-Countryside/Penarth-Pier-Pavilion/About-us.aspx",
      "inspection": "Current operator read:1929 pavilion, vaulted main gallery and current cultural venue. Supports surviving named structure, not physical survey."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.valeofglamorgan.gov.uk/en/our_council/press_and_communications/latest_news/2023/February/New-lighting-and-decking-to-be-installed-at-Penarth-Pier-Pavilion.aspx",
      "inspection": "Operator2023 maintenance read: replacement of lower deck/upper balcony boards in keeping with main pier plus new lighting. Geometry remains selected restored form; temporary lighting/closures not claimed."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@51.4351,-3.1665,19z/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "inspection": "Aerial individually inspected: ESE pier, white four-dome pavilion with long zinc roof/ridge/four south dormers, convex seaward terraces, low curving shore shop wings, paired middeck shelters, broad open head/ticket hut and narrow lower landing edge. Own outline distinct from promenade/baths/apartments."
    }
  ],
